{"parentUuid":"db15629b-d455-4247-96ca-650983c87585","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BinEgGkQMhMavX8wtBu3ny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qe2LvDZtjahZaaUD7tzRwS","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"large CP problem SAT encoding 100000 variables CNF size scaling experience"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5623,"cache_read_input_tokens":21019,"output_tokens":312,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5623},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":21019,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5623,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caootce6RvZb3nFptaLEV","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ca1befae-afa8-4b12-9c8e-cef3a74c858c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:22.822Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a4f03231-3190-4952-91bc-780e5b1319e8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014YAqibbZnBj449Pe6NEhMc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP no-overlap rectangle packing SAT encoding direct order log encoding comparison clauses\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Log-Support Encoding of CSP into SAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221633034_The_Log-Support_Encoding_of_CSP_into_SAT\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A SAT-based Method for Solving the Two-dimensional Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220445013_A_SAT-based_Method_for_Solving_the_Two-dimensional_Strip_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"Proposal and Evaluation of Hybrid Encoding of CSP to SAT Integrating Order and Log Encodings | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/314133918_Proposal_and_Evaluation_of_Hybrid_Encoding_of_CSP_to_SAT_Integrating_Order_and_Log_Encodings\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A SAT Encoding for Multi-dimensional Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221353572_A_SAT_Encoding_for_Multi-dimensional_Packing_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"SciELO Brazil - EFFICIENT SAT AND MAXSAT TECHNIQUES FOR SOLVING THE TWO-DIMENSIONAL STRIP PACKING PROBLEM EFFICIENT SAT AND MAXSAT TECHNIQUES FOR SOLVING THE TWO-DIMENSIONAL STRIP PACKING PROBLEM\",\"url\":\"http://www.scielo.br/j/pope/a/Cz3GM6VVxJRB4XhXFHXW8Br/?lang=en\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"A SAT-based Method for Solving the Two-dimensional Strip Packing problem\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/p/potassco/mailman/attachment/1323943585.4102.431.camel@white.sevalidation.com/1/\"},{\"title\":\"Computing Science Group THE ORDER ENCODING: FROM TRACTABLE CSP TO TRACTABLE SAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/files/4014/maxclosed_orderencoding_v16_TR.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about SAT encodings for rectangle packing problems. Here are the key findings:\n\n## SAT Encodings for No-Overlap Rectangle Packing\n\nThe two-dimensional strip packing problem (2SPP) can be solved by translating it to SAT problems through a SAT encoding called order encoding.\n\n### Order Encoding vs. Log Encoding\n\nThe order encoding maintains bound consistency by unit propagation and works well for constraints consisting of small/middle sized arity and variable domains. The log encoding generates smaller CNF and works well for constraints consisting of larger sized arity and variable domains but its performance is not good in general because more inference steps are required to ripple carries.\n\n### Hybrid Approach\n\nA hybrid approach has been developed that hybridizes the order and log encodings without channeling constraints, where each variable is encoded by either the order encoding or the log encoding, and each constraint can contain both types of variables. The hybrid encoding solves the largest number of instances with the shortest CPU time compared to order and log encodings alone.\n\n### Clause Complexity Comparison\n\nIn comparing direct encoding with order encoding, the order encoding requires fewer SAT clauses while the direct encoding requires 15 clauses. Additionally, Boolean variables encoding position thresholds facilitate a compact representation of comparison constraints.\n\nThe search results indicate that order encoding is generally preferred over direct encoding for rectangle packing problems due to better clause efficiency and propagation properties, though log encoding can be competitive when optimized.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e3879900-3847-47be-a0ac-2d7b5a020f74","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:27.772Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a4f03231-3190-4952-91bc-780e5b1319e8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bca0e079-c52e-43f4-abb4-0249aa307479","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AB4oW6txNGdixmveYAs7E5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Picat MiniZinc fzn2cnf SAT backend integer variable encoding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MiniZinc with Picat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minizinc/c/mBmQL6gXKP0\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints\",\"url\":\"http://www.picat-lang.org/papers/cp17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PicatSAT: A SAT Compiler in Picat\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_picatsat.txt\"},{\"title\":\"The Picat-SAT Compiler Neng-Fa Zhou1 and H˚akan Kjellerstrand2\",\"url\":\"http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/padl16.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-66158-2_43\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Picat-SAT Compiler\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/305780906_The_Picat-SAT_Compiler\"},{\"title\":\"From MiniZinc to Optimization Modulo Theories, and Back (Extended Version) | DeepAI\",\"url\":\"https://deepai.org/publication/from-minizinc-to-optimization-modulo-theories-and-back-extended-version\"},{\"title\":\"How to use Picat to create CNF files from Minizinc files? - Code Thinking\",\"url\":\"https://www.00w5.com/article/d56866b725923bf082c35bda2f82ee17.html\"},{\"title\":\"In Pursuit of an Eﬃcient SAT Encoding for the Hamiltonian Cycle Problem\",\"url\":\"http://www.picat-lang.org/papers/cp20.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc Challenge scores on benchmarks that do not use global constraints | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/MiniZinc-Challenge-scores-on-benchmarks-that-do-not-use-global-constraints_tbl2_305780906\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Picat, MiniZinc, fzn2cnf, SAT backend, and integer variable encoding:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Picat and MiniZinc Integration:**\nPicat can be configured as a solver in MiniZinc through the fzn_picat_sat.pi module, which processes FlatZinc files. Users can convert MiniZinc files to FlatZinc using mzn2fzn, then convert the result to CNF using modified versions of fzn_picat_sat.pi.\n\n**Integer Variable Encoding:**\nPicat employs log-encoding for compiling domain variables and constraints, using log₂(n) Boolean variables for a domain with maximum absolute value n, plus another Boolean variable if the domain contains both negative and positive values.\n\n**PicatSAT Compiler:**\nPicat-SAT adopts the sign-and-magnitude log-encoding for domain variables. PicatSAT adopts optimizations from CP systems, language compilers, and hardware design systems for encoding constraints into compact and efficient SAT code, and is empowered by equivalence reasoning for arithmetic constraints.\n\n**Performance:**\nPicatSAT won the main tracks in the XCSP3 Competition 2019 and 2022, and has ranked highly in every MiniZinc Challenge since 2016.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ed66cc09-ebee-4f66-a409-3a190110ed0e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:27.807Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bca0e079-c52e-43f4-abb4-0249aa307479","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"db15629b-d455-4247-96ca-650983c87585","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XW2cUbdTkNcteusGgCVUz3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy DIMACS export to_cnf cardinality constraint Boolean\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DIMACS (cpmpy.tools.dimacs) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/complex_sudoku_examples/api/tools/dimacs.html\"},{\"title\":\"DIMACS (cpmpy.tools.dimacs) — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/var-comp-sum/api/tools/dimacs.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.transformations.to_cnf — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_modules/cpmpy/transformations/to_cnf.html\"},{\"title\":\"Convert boolean expressions to cnf (cpmpy.transformations.to_cnf) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/transformations/to_cnf.html\"},{\"title\":\"Convert boolean expressions to cnf (cpmpy.transformations.to_cnf) — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cpm_array_order/api/transformations/to_cnf.html\"},{\"title\":\"Boolean formula manipulation (pysat.formula) — PySAT 1.9.dev2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/formula.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT Documentation Release 1.9.dev2\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/pysat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efﬁcient CNF Encoding of Boolean Cardinality Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~fbacchus/csc2512/Assignments/Bailleux-Boufkhad2003_Chapter_EfficientCNFEncodingOfBooleanC.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient CNF Encoding of Boolean Cardinality Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-45193-8_8\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/solvers/pysat.html\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for your query about CPMpy DIMACS export with to_cnf and cardinality constraints:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**DIMACS Format and CPMpy:**\nCPMpy implements helper functions for exporting models from and to DIMACS format, where DIMACS is a textual format to represent CNF problems. An integer represents a Boolean variable and a negative Boolean variable is represented using a - sign.\n\n**CNF Transformation:**\nThe write_dimacs function writes CPMpy models to DIMACS format using the \"to_cnf\" transformation from CPMpy. The conversion process flattens global constraints that are is_bool() and not in supported using the tseitin transform.\n\n**Cardinality Constraints in Extended Formats:**\nWhile standard DIMACS only supports basic CNF clauses, extended formats like CNFPlus support native cardinality constraints provided by solvers like MiniCard. Native cardinality constraints of CNF+ cannot be translated to SMT-LIB2 unless an explicit cardinality encoding is applied.\n\nThe search results indicate that CPMpy uses the Pindakaas library for its to_cnf transformation, which can handle various constraint types including cardinality constraints by encoding them into standard CNF clauses suitable for DIMACS format.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"01f440a3-cc99-4d44-8842-9ec79b103862","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:28.710Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db15629b-d455-4247-96ca-650983c87585","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ca1befae-afa8-4b12-9c8e-cef3a74c858c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qe2LvDZtjahZaaUD7tzRwS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"large CP problem SAT encoding 100000 variables CNF size scaling experience\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How to improve CP-SAT performance for large bin-packing problems? · Issue #1799 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints\",\"url\":\"http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/cp17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient CNF Encoding for Selecting 1 from N Objects\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~wklieber/papers/2007_efficient-cnf-encoding-for-selecting-1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Robust CNF Encodings of Cardinality Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://sat.inesc-id.pt/~ines/publications/cp07.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319231476_Optimizing_SAT_Encodings_for_Arithmetic_Constraints\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Encodings into SAT Combinatorial Problem Solving (CPS)\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.upc.edu/~erodri/webpage/cps/theory/sat/encodings/slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture Notes on SAT Encodings\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~15414/s21/lectures/13-sat-encodings.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding large CP problems, SAT encoding, and CNF size scaling:\n\n## CNF Size Scaling and Encoding Approaches\n\nThe research shows that there's a fundamental tradeoff in SAT encodings between the number of clauses and auxiliary variables:\n\nWhen encoding a problem into SAT, there is usually a tradeoff between reducing the number of clauses and increasing the number of variables.\n\n## Cardinality Constraint Encodings\n\nFor large-scale problems, different encoding strategies have different complexity characteristics:\n\n- A naive encoding of \"at most one\" constraints requires O(n²) CNF clauses, while alternative encodings require only O(n) clauses at the expense of O(n) extra variables.\n\n- Encodings for cardinality constraints can be linear, logarithmic or quadratic in the number of variables.\n\n## Practical Experience with Large Problems\n\nOne documented case involved a bin-packing optimization model with 51,051 variables (50,000 binary variables) and 100,000 linear constraints.\n\nUsing naive encodings for large Sudoku (81×81) generates huge CNF, and the runtime of SAT solvers becomes unmanageable if the input formula size is on the order of gigabytes.\n\n## Optimization Strategies\n\nEquivalence reasoning reduces code sizes, and for some benchmarks, significantly reduces the solving time. Hybrid encoding approaches that use both order and log encodings have been shown to solve the largest number of instances with the shortest CPU time.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5d46e890-a587-4e71-82a2-040fb2090070","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:30.166Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca1befae-afa8-4b12-9c8e-cef3a74c858c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zoo