{"parentUuid":"16c82ec5-145f-40be-9c59-afcd937accee","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VLoKUi5JDQc6Cyo9Af7YKB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V5AWurj4KQgRtgDfPFpXRc","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed","prompt":"What constraints does Chuffed support? How does it compare to OR-Tools CP-SAT for large grid problems? Any benchmark numbers for problems with 100k+ variables?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4329,"cache_read_input_tokens":32612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4329,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoova2dnWqFt6jVqVszn","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2812b64-4cbf-48f8-9555-98b8df94d89e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:48.739Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f2812b64-4cbf-48f8-9555-98b8df94d89e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VLoKUi5JDQc6Cyo9Af7YKB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nmv9vtUXtVxAXkFS2Loemj","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"http://www.picat-lang.org/papers/cp17.pdf","prompt":"What are the SAT encoding sizes (variables and clauses) for arithmetic constraints in PicatSAT? Specific numbers for log encoding vs order encoding blow-up factor?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4329,"cache_read_input_tokens":32612,"output_tokens":378,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4329},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":32612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4329,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoova2dnWqFt6jVqVszn","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e340772b-4c7b-474d-a65f-d162dc742c5f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:50.592Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f2812b64-4cbf-48f8-9555-98b8df94d89e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V5AWurj4KQgRtgDfPFpXRc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Chuffed Constraints and Performance\n\nBased on the GitHub repository content provided, I can address your questions:\n\n## Supported Constraints\n\nChuffed implements several global propagators including: \"alldiff, inverse, minimum, table, regular, mdd, cumulative, disjunctive, circuit, difference.\"\n\nThe solver supports two variable types: small integer variables (domain represented as byte string) and large integers (represented by bounds only, without holes).\n\n## Comparison with OR-Tools CP-SAT\n\nThe documentation does not contain any information comparing Chuffed to OR-Tools CP-SAT or performance metrics for that comparison.\n\n## Benchmarks for Large Problems\n\nNo benchmark data is provided in this repository content for problems with 100,000+ variables. The page mentions that \"the search reduction, however, can reach orders of magnitude on appropriate problems\" when using lazy clause generation, but specific numerical benchmarks for large-scale instances aren't included.\n\n**Recommendation:** To find performance comparisons and benchmarks, you would need to consult published research papers on Chuffed, or contact the development team directly through the GitHub repository's issues section."}]},"uuid":"cf8b475d-8500-4a0e-8123-086f3b6a2de5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:54.069Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2812b64-4cbf-48f8-9555-98b8df94d89e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"16c82ec5-145f-40be-9c59-afcd937accee","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MAPbDFifGbnu5yWeNxLikg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"order encoding\" integer variable domain size SAT variables formula clauses count\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Encoding Linear Constraints into SAT Ignasi Ab´ıo1 and Peter J. Stuckey1,2\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp2014a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Some Tips of Implementing Order Encoding\",\"url\":\"https://cspsat.gitlab.io/sugar/docs/order-encoding/\"},{\"title\":\"Computing Science Group THE ORDER ENCODING: FROM TRACTABLE CSP TO TRACTABLE SAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/files/4014/maxclosed_orderencoding_v16_TR.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Sugar: A CSP to SAT Translator Based on Order Encoding\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/CPAI06/descriptionSolvers/Sugar.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture Notes on SAT Encodings\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~15414/s21/lectures/13-sat-encodings.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Order Encoding: From Tractable CSP to Tractable SAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220944335_The_Order_Encoding_From_Tractable_CSP_to_Tractable_SAT\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Hybrid Encoding of CSP to SAT Integrating Order and Log Encodings\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304288091_A_Hybrid_Encoding_of_CSP_to_SAT_Integrating_Order_and_Log_Encodings\"},{\"title\":\"Abacus: A New Hybrid Encoding for SAT Problems\",\"url\":\"https://univ-angers.hal.science/hal-03385029/document\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Compiling Pseudo-Boolean Constraints to SAT with Order Encoding\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/271555248_Compiling_Pseudo-Boolean_Constraints_to_SAT_with_Order_Encoding\"},{\"title\":\"Linear Ordering in the SAT Encoding of the All-Different Constraint over Bit-Vectors – Association for Logic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.nmsu.edu/ALP/2015/03/linear-ordering-in-the-sat-encoding-of-the-all-different-constraint-over-bit-vectors/\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for your query about order encoding, integer variable domain size, SAT variables, formula clauses, and count:\n\n## Order Encoding Overview\n\nThe order encoding (sometimes called ladder or regular) introduces Boolean variables yi for 0 ⩽ i < d for an integer variable y with domain [0, d], where a variable yi is true iff y ≤ i.\n\n## Variables and Domain Size\n\nIt is sufficient to assign propositional variables for each x ≤ dj (1 ≤ j < n) instead of assigning for each value d where d1 ≤ d < dn, where the domain of variable x is {d1, d2, ..., dn}.\n\n## Clauses and Formula Size\n\nComparisons of the form ∑ ai xi ≤ b can be encoded into O(d^(m-1)) clauses in general where d is the domain size. However, it is possible to reduce the number of integer variables in each comparison to at most three by introducing new integer variables, so each comparison ∑ ai xi ≤ b can be encoded by at most O(m d²) clauses even when m ≥ 4.\n\n## Limitations\n\nIn some cases, however, the domains of the integer variables are too large for order encoding. For addressing this, in the compact order encoding, each integer variable is represented by using a numeral system of base B≥2 and each digit is encoded by using the order encoding.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7d3278d2-595f-435b-ac4a-d9607b5db97a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:55.082Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16c82ec5-145f-40be-9c59-afcd937accee","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e340772b-4c7b-474d-a65f-d162dc742c5f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nmv9vtUXtVxAXkFS2Loemj","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot find specific information about SAT encoding sizes (variables and clauses) for arithmetic constraints in PicatSAT, or comparisons between log encoding versus order encoding blow-up factors, in the provided PDF document.\n\nThe document appears to be a technical paper, but the content visible in the excerpt does not contain the numerical specifications you're requesting regarding encoding complexity metrics.\n\nTo obtain this information, I'd recommend:\n1. Checking the paper's main sections on constraint encoding\n2. Reviewing any tables or figures comparing encoding methods\n3. Consulting PicatSAT's technical documentation directly\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 316.2KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778184352696-u4f6s0.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"367fa5c4-a55f-4744-be19-b2536d4c7d0a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:55.899Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e340772b-4c7b-474d-a65f-d162dc742c5f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
