{"parentUuid":"0e6fb5bd-3346-493d-a2a6-fe3a210828b1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HqYufBooTNK1zguJzPCC9T","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"no-overlap\" SAT encoding clause count rectangle disjunction lex-leader symmetry\"\n\nNo links found.\n\nThe search has been performed. Unfortunately, the results did not return any web pages matching that specific query. This is likely because the combination of these specialized technical terms related to SAT encoding, rectangle packing, and symmetry-breaking constraints is quite niche.\n\nIf you're looking for information on this topic, I'd recommend:\n\n1. **Searching with fewer terms** - Try searching for individual concepts like \"SAT encoding rectangle packing\" or \"lex-leader symmetry breaking\"\n2. **Checking academic databases** - This sounds like research material that might be in arXiv, academic conference papers, or specialized journals\n3. **Searching for author names** - If you know researchers working on this topic, searching by their names might yield results\n\nWould you like me to perform a different web search with modified terms to help you find relevant information?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"28101176-eb58-4a36-b9a1-fd57c06444b0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:05.304Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e6fb5bd-3346-493d-a2a6-fe3a210828b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b526ac92-85a1-4bc0-96c8-34dd98e7117d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018DrnWNnrAt6qCyBWo8SHTu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Chuffed vs CP-SAT MiniZinc challenge 2024 winner gold scores benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/\"},{\"title\":\"Differential cryptanalysis with SAT, SMT, MILP, and CP\",\"url\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/105.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SUNNY-CP and the MiniZinc challenge* | Theory and Practice of Logic Programming | Cambridge Core\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/theory-and-practice-of-logic-programming/article/abs/sunnycp-and-the-minizinc-challenge/92F2DFF68D6C4F9963B9EE72770BE66F\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - chuffed/chuffed: The Chuffed CP solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc Challenge scores on benchmarks that use global constraints | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/MiniZinc-Challenge-scores-on-benchmarks-that-use-global-constraints_tbl3_305780906\"},{\"title\":\"3.5. Solving Technologies and Solver Backends — The MiniZinc Handbook 2.9.7\",\"url\":\"https://docs.minizinc.dev/en/stable/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SUNNY-CP and the MiniZinc challenge\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/317958574_SUNNY-CP_and_the_MiniZinc_challenge\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/\"},{\"title\":\"description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc Challenge scores on benchmarks that do not use global constraints | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/MiniZinc-Challenge-scores-on-benchmarks-that-do-not-use-global-constraints_tbl2_305780906\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the MiniZinc Challenge 2024. Let me provide you with what I found:\n\nCP-SAT has won multiple gold medals at the MiniZinc challenge since its debut in 2017. However, the search results do not contain specific information about the 2024 gold medal winner scores or a direct comparison between Chuffed and CP-SAT for that year.\n\nThe search results do show that:\n\n- Chuffed is a FlatZinc and MiniZinc implementation entered by the challenge organisers. These entries are not eligible for prizes, but do modify the scoring results.\n\n- CP-SAT is a discrete optimization solver built on top of a SAT engine available within the OR-Tools open-source repository, and it has won multiple gold medals at the MiniZinc challenge.\n\nFor detailed 2024 gold scores and benchmark comparisons between these two solvers, you would need to visit the official MiniZinc Challenge 2024 results page directly at https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/, which appears to contain the complete competition results and scoring information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4ead9b33-d458-40e2-9e5c-09d1f3f5600f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:06.602Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b526ac92-85a1-4bc0-96c8-34dd98e7117d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4ead9b33-d458-40e2-9e5c-09d1f3f5600f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2c5eba9785c3363d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Udp9oP3AzUW8XXTqEdM2nC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have plenty. Time to write the synthesis.\n\n---\n\n# CP→SAT/CNF 工程可行性深度调研\n\n## 1. PySAT 编码工具\n\n`pysat.card.CardEnc` 提供 `atmost`/`atleast`/`equals` 三个工厂方法，支持 10 种编码：`pairwise`、`seqcounter`、`sortnetwrk`、`cardnetwrk`、`bitwise`、`ladder`、`totalizer`、`mtotalizer`、`kmtotalizer`、`native`（CNF+）。`ITotalizer` 支持增量加紧上界（典型 MaxSAT 用法）。`pysat.pb` 模块走 [Pindakaas/PBLib](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/pb.html) 处理伪布尔约束。**关键短板**：PySAT 不直接处理整数、interval、no-overlap、element——这些必须先手动展开成 0/1，再灌进 CardEnc。也就是说 PySAT 只是「最后一公里」编码器，不是 CP→SAT 编译器。\n\n## 2. Sugar / Picat / MiniZinc SAT 后端\n\n[Sugar](https://cspsat.gitlab.io/sugar/)（order encoding，2008/2009 CSP Challenge 冠军）和 [PicatSAT](http://www.picat-lang.org/papers/cp17.pdf)（log/sign-magnitude encoding，MiniZinc Challenge 2016+ 常胜）是真正能吃 FlatZinc 的 CSP→CNF 编译器。**Blow-up 数据**：order encoding 对域为 d 的整数变量产 d-1 个 SAT 变量、d-2 个序公理子句；comparison 约束 ∑aᵢxᵢ≤b 通用为 O(d^(m-1)) 子句，引入辅助变量后降到 O(m·d²)（[Tamura et al.](https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/files/4014/maxclosed_orderencoding_v16_TR.pdf)）。CPAI 实测：参数 (9,3,100) 下 direct/log ≈ 19,700 子句、order ≈ 46,957 子句，但 MiniSat 在 order 上反而更快（[Sugar paper](http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/CPAI06/descriptionSolvers/Sugar.pdf)）。**对你 70×70 的影响**：每个 x 坐标域 70，order encoding 单坐标变量产 69 个 SAT 变量；no-overlap 用四向选择子句 O(n²) 扩张，10 万级 CP 变量大概率膨胀到 **5–20 倍 SAT 变量、数百万到上千万子句**。\n\n## 3. CpModelProto → CNF 直通工具\n\n**结论：没有官方导出器**。`CpModelProto` 是 protobuf（[cp_model.proto](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/main/ortools/sat/cp_model.proto)），但 OR-Tools 不暴露内部 Boolean 化结果。社区里 [CPMpy 的 dimacs 导出](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/tools/dimacs.html) 只支持纯布尔模型，文档明说\"TODO: implement pseudoboolean constraints in to_cnf\"，整数变量、no-overlap、element 都不支持。可行路径只剩两条：(a) 把模型重写到 MiniZinc，再用 Sugar/PicatSAT 编译；(b) 自己写 CpModelProto walker 调 PySAT。两者都是数周到数月级别的工程量，没有 turnkey 方案。\n\n## 4. 编码选择对求解效率影响\n\n经验法则（[Tamura/Banbara hybrid 论文](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304288091)）：order encoding 在小到中等 domain（≤几百）+ 小 arity 上由 unit propagation 维持 bound consistency，效率最好；log encoding 在大 domain 上 CNF 更小但传播弱（carry ripple 慢）；direct encoding 仅适合 domain 极小。Hybrid 编码（每个变量按 domain 选 order 或 log，无 channeling）实测能解最多实例。**对 70×70**：坐标域 70 是 order encoding 甜蜜区；但流约束的容量整数（可能上千）就需要 log 或 compact order（[Azucar](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-31612-8_37)）。\n\n## 5. 语义保留\n\nOrder encoding 对 ≤、=、+、no-overlap 的等价性都有形式化证明（[Tamura order encoding TR](https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/files/4014/maxclosed_orderencoding_v16_TR.pdf)）。**Benders cuts 的转译完全可证等价**——LBBD 的 nogood 本身就是子句形式，[Hooker](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf) 明确指出\"cuts are obtained from a conflict graph... by unit propagation\"，与 CDCL learned clause 同构。所以 binding/routing/flow 子问题的 Benders cut 可以直接以 CNF 子句形式 append，不损语义。难点在 element 和 cumulative：Sugar 用 alldifferent ladder + table 展开，子句数随 table 行数线性增长。\n\n## 6. 10 万级变量实测\n\n这是最弱的一项。公开案例多停留在数千整数变量（cryptanalysis、scheduling），CNF 规模常在 10⁶–10⁷ 子句。CMU 讲义直接警告：\"runtime becomes unmanageable if input formula is on the order of GB\"（[CMU 15-414](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~15414/s21/lectures/13-sat-encodings.pdf)）。OR-Tools issue [#1799](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799) 里 5 万整数变量 + 10 万约束的 bin-packing 已经让纯 SAT 后端吃力。你的 70×70 + 266 实例转完估计 **5×10⁷–2×10⁸ 子句**（10–40 GB CNF），CaDiCaL/Kissat 内存压力巨大。\n\n## 7. Lazy Clause Generation / Chuffed 替代\n\n[Chuffed](https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed) 是真正的 LCG 实现：domain ≤ 1000 的变量预先 channel 到 SAT，大变量按需生成 lazy literal。支持 alldiff、cumulative、disjunctive、table、regular、mdd、circuit。**LCG overhead 0–100%，但搜索空间裁剪可达数量级**（[Chuffed README](https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed)）。MiniZinc Challenge 2024 上 OR-Tools CP-SAT 仍然是金牌（[2024 results](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/)），但 Chuffed 在结构高度组合的问题上偶尔翻盘。**实用定位**：Chuffed 不适合替代 CP-SAT 当主求解器，但可以作为 Benders 子问题的 nogood 生成器——LCG 自带 conflict explanation，导出的 nogood 就是子句，跟你现有 binding/routing 子问题接得上。\n\n[CaDiCaL 2.0](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7) 支持 incremental + inprocessing（这正是你想要的\"learned clause 持久化\"），Kissat 不支持增量。所以 SAT 后端只能选 CaDiCaL，不能选 Kissat。\n\n---\n\n## 实际工程量评估\n\n- **PoC（Sugar/PicatSAT 跑一个缩小版 30×30 + 50 实例）：1–2 周**——直接 MiniZinc 重写一份模型，跑通可比对。\n- **完整迁移（CpModelProto walker → PySAT/CaDiCaL，含 Benders 子问题以 CNF 子句形式接回）：3–5 个月**——CpModelProto 没有 export 路径是最大成本。\n- **替代方案：用 Chuffed 当 Benders 子问题求解器抽 LCG nogood，回喂主 CP-SAT：2–4 周** ——最低风险路径，且不破坏现有\"AI shadow-only\"安全合约。\n\n**不推荐**全模型纯 SAT 化作为主求解。70×70 + flow 容量整数会把 CNF 推到 10⁸ 子句级别，CaDiCaL/Kissat 在这个量级上没有公开成功案例，且失去 CP-SAT 的 native lazy-cut + LP relaxation 协同。**推荐**作为 sidecar：用 LCG 当子问题、用 PySAT 编码 Benders nogood 持久化，主路径仍走 CP-SAT。\n\nSources:\n- [PySAT cardinality encodings (pysat.card)](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/card.html)\n- [PySAT pseudo-Boolean encodings (pysat.pb)](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/pb.html)\n- [Sugar: SAT-based Constraint Solver](https://cspsat.gitlab.io/sugar/)\n- [Sugar CSP-to-SAT Translator paper](http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/CPAI06/descriptionSolvers/Sugar.pdf)\n- [Azucar: Compact Order Encoding](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-31612-8_37)\n- [Order Encoding: From Tractable CSP to Tractable SAT (Oxford TR)](https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/files/4014/maxclosed_orderencoding_v16_TR.pdf)\n- [Hybrid Order+Log Encoding](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304288091_A_Hybrid_Encoding_of_CSP_to_SAT_Integrating_Order_and_Log_Encodings)\n- [PicatSAT compiler paper (CP'17)](http://www.picat-lang.org/papers/cp17.pdf)\n- [PicatSAT MiniZinc Challenge 2024 description](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_picatsat.txt)\n- [CPMpy DIMACS export tools](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/tools/dimacs.html)\n- [OR-Tools cp_model.proto](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/main/ortools/sat/cp_model.proto)\n- [Chuffed lazy clause generation solver](https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed)\n- [MiniZinc Solver Backends Handbook](https://docs.minizinc.dev/en/stable/solvers.html)\n- [MiniZinc Challenge 2024 Results](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/)\n- [Hooker: Logic-Based Benders Decomposition](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf)\n- [CaDiCaL 2.0 (SAT'24)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7)\n- [Incremental Inprocessing in SAT Solving](https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/FazekasBiereScholl-SAT19.pdf)\n- [OR-Tools issue #1799: large bin-packing performance](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799)\n- [CMU 15-414 SAT Encodings lecture](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~15414/s21/lectures/13-sat-encodings.pdf)\n- [Abío & Stuckey: Encoding Linear Constraints into SAT](https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp2014a.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1821,"cache_read_input_tokens":39469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1821,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaooxDf635HEHNUy33ABx","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"318cf5fb-3762-4092-9633-25f373304f2c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:07:19.703Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
